Use the tested GMAC1 TX tap for the LubanCat 2 V2 JLSemi PHY.

On the tested board the PHY already enables its internal 2 ns TX delay.
The vendor MAC TX tap of 0x22 causes gigabit packet loss and peer RX FCS
errors. A zero MAC TX tap eliminates those errors in the tested link,
including a 60-second TCP download at 929 Mbit/s without retransmissions.

Keep RX at 0x07 and retain RGMII mode. The RK3568 glue driver keeps its
TX delay enable bit set even with a zero tap, matching the runtime test.
GMAC0 timing is unchanged.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-lubancat-2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-lubancat-2.dts
@@ -506,7 +506,8 @@
 		     &gmac1m1_rgmii_clk
 		     &gmac1m1_rgmii_bus>;
 
-	tx_delay = <0x22>;
+	/* The JLSemi PHY provides an internal TX delay. */
+	tx_delay = <0x00>;
 	rx_delay = <0x07>;
 
 	phy-handle = <&rgmii_phy1>;
